  "market_commentary": {
    "overview": "",
    "bulkers": "The dry cargo market continues to demonstrate strength, maintaining firm levels. The Baltic \nDry Index (BDI) reached a multi-year peak of 3,628 points last Friday, before slightly declining to 3,507 \npoints today: \n \nBaltic Dry Index           3507   -14 \nBaltic Capesize Index   6080   -42 \nBaltic Panamax Index   2407   -2 \nBaltic Supramax Index 1719   +6 \nBaltic Handysize Index   940   +9 \n \nThe S+P market remains very firm and active with 21 recorded transactions, comprising 2 kamsarmaxes, \n3 panamax, 3 ultramax, 4 Supramaxes & 9 Handysize bulk carriers. For a detailed review and additional \ninformation regarding these week's transactions, kindly refer to our \"representative sales\" section.",
    "demolition": "The Subcontinent markets remain stable but with a subdued outlook. In Bangladesh, most \nshipyards are operating at full capacity, whereas Pakistan is witnessing a decline in local steel prices. \nIndia stands out as the most active market this week due to robust demand for tonnage. For an overview \nof demolition market rates, please check our comprehensive demometer below:"
  },
